<article class="env-definition" id="0FFY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FFY">Definition <span data-tag="0FFY">4.43.15</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{C}'$ be symmetric monoidal categories. A <em>functor of symmetric monoidal categories</em> $F : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}'$ is given by a functor $F$ as indicated and an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F(X) \otimes F(Y) \to F(X \otimes Y)  \]
</div>
  <p> functorial in $X$ and $Y$ such that $F$ is a functor of monoidal categories and such that for all objects $X$ and $Y$ the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ F(X) \otimes F(Y) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  F(X \otimes Y) \ar[d] \\  F(Y) \otimes F(X) \ar[r] &  F(Y \otimes X) }  \]
</div>
  <p> commutes. </p>
</article>